id: mem-a65205fd
name: Agent create defaults to project scope
description: >-
  paradigm agent create defaults to project-local, requires --global for global agents. Document
  this clearly — most users want global.



  `paradigm agent create <id>` saves to `.paradigm/agents/` (project-local) by default.

  `paradigm agent create <id> --global` saves to `~/.paradigm/agents/` (global).


  **Why:** Most users expect agents to persist across projects. The default is counterintuitive.


  **How to apply:** When writing docs, README, or agent-related help text, always show the
  `--global` flag prominently. The README's custom agent example should use `~/.paradigm/agents/`
  (the global path). Agent guides should lead with global creation and mention project-scoping as an
  advanced override.
category: documentation
trigger: postflight
severity: advisory
check:
  type: context-checked
  params: {}
enabled: false
